From: gpu-nvidia-fix <https://github.com/wintermoot/gpu-nvidia-fix>
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] nvidia-modeset: replace removed strncpy() in nvkms_strncpy

Kernel 7.2 removed strncpy() from the kernel API. nvkms_strncpy is a
wrapper whose contract returns the destination pointer. strscpy()
returns a length instead, so the call is split and dest is returned
explicitly.

Applies to nvidia-580.173.02.

--- a/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -640,8 +640,9 @@ int nvkms_strcmp(const char *s1, const char *s2)
 {
     return strcmp(s1, s2);
 }

 char* nvkms_strncpy(char *dest, const char *src, size_t n)
 {
-    return strncpy(dest, src, n);
+    strscpy(dest, src, n);
+    return dest;
 }
